WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:01.890
- We always like to wrap things up

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.990
with something that could
bring you some extra joy,

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.250
especially during the holidays.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.742
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:06.742 --> 00:00:08.649
(punchy intro music)

00:00:08.649 --> 00:00:09.990
(audience applauds)

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.750
You may remember last year
we had some educators here

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.550
so obsessed with Christmas movies

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.150
they launched their very own
podcast, Deck the Hallmark.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.290
It's awesome.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.760
Every year, they watch dozens

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.710
and dozens of Hallmark holiday movies

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.380
and break them down from
differing viewpoints.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.390
It's become wildly popular.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.104
Now they've taken it a step further.

00:00:29.104 --> 00:00:31.560
The two main hosts have a new kids book

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.830
I think every parent watching
will appreciate and recognize.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.697
It's called "When's It
Gonna Be Christmas Again?!"

00:00:36.697 --> 00:00:37.710
(audience laughs)

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.080
So I caught up with Bran
and Dan the other day.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.133
So check this out.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:43.763
- Hey.

00:00:43.763 --> 00:00:44.774
- Hey, hey, hey.

00:00:44.774 --> 00:00:45.690
- How's it going?

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.523
- What's up y'all?

00:00:46.523 --> 00:00:47.760
So Bran, I'm gonna start with you.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.809
So how's the holiday movie
viewing going this year?

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:52.440
- I'd be lying, Kelly,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.600
if I didn't say it was
a little overwhelming.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.850
Would it shock you to find out that

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.890
across all of the networks

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.640
there's 200 plus new Christmas movies

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.680
just for this holiday season?

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.910
It's overwhelming.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.110
We're not covering all of them.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.184
We're covering about 60 of
them, which I'm still proud of-

00:01:10.184 --> 00:01:11.017
- Very proud of.

00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:12.600
- 60 movies in two months is a lot.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.440
We've brought on some extra
people to help us do that, but-

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.273
- That's a lot.

00:01:15.273 --> 00:01:16.200
- There's a lot of Christmas movies

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.887
but a lot of fun to be had, for sure.

00:01:17.887 --> 00:01:20.760
- Oh my. Yeah, that's a
Christmas movie a day, man.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.035
Yeah. So Dan, tell us
about the new kids book.

00:01:23.035 --> 00:01:25.740
- Yeah, it's called "When's
It Gonna Be Christmas Again?!"

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.180
And it basically takes you

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.030
through an entire year with
a family where the kids,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.590
no matter what holiday
they're celebrating,

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.500
they always just ask, "When's
it gonna be Christmas again?"

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.491
And, you know,

00:01:35.491 --> 00:01:38.880
it can be exhausting as a
parent to hear that all year,

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.300
but this book is about
taking a minute to stop

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.150
and to really see the joy in that.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.238
I've got twin six-year-old boys

00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:49.230
who are just the light of my life,

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.670
and they love Christmas.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.860
And so, between those two and Brand,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.696
they always ask "when's it
gonna be Christmas again?"

00:01:54.696 --> 00:01:55.529
- Right.

00:01:55.529 --> 00:01:57.750
- And so, this book was an opportunity and

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.830
the illustrations in the
book are inspired by my kids.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.200
For us to see what it's like as parents,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.910
where your perspective kind of shifts,

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:10.910
to say "Oh my goodness. This
opportunity to see the joy

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:11.910
in these kids' faces,

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.430
even when it's not time for
Christmas, is wonderful."

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.310
And so, you can have the spirit
of Christmas all year long

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.140
by looking through the lens of a child.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.180
And so, we're really proud of the book

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.821
and that's what it's about.

00:02:22.821 --> 00:02:23.785
(audience applauds)

00:02:23.785 --> 00:02:27.415
- I love those guys and I'm
liking the post right now.

00:02:27.415 --> 00:02:29.220
(bell dings)

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.500
So remember to check
out "Deck the Hallmark"

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.970
wherever you get your podcasts.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.740
It's really good. You should check it out.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.270
Now I'm about to do
something I know someone

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.040
in our audience will be liking.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.170
That's because, usually
at this point in the hour,

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.057
we give our guest a
thousand dollars courtesy

00:02:42.057 --> 00:02:43.980
of our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.490
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.040
But today, someone here is getting it.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.140
It's actually taped
below one of your seats,

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.254
so you might wanna take a look.

00:02:54.254 --> 00:02:55.087
(drum roll plays)

00:02:55.087 --> 00:02:56.500
Yeah.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.583
Who wants it?

00:02:58.890 --> 00:02:59.723
Yeah!

00:03:01.076 --> 00:03:03.146
(congratulatory music)

00:03:03.146 --> 00:03:05.521
(audience applauds)

00:03:05.521 --> 00:03:06.901
What's your name?

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.130
- Megan.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.930
- What do you think you're
gonna do with the money?

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.317
- Oh, you don't even know.

00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:12.150
(Megan laughs)

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.040
- Oh, you're gonna do
fun things with it. Okay.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:14.873
- I am, well...

00:03:14.873 --> 00:03:17.130
I don't have a car and I just
lost part of a job yesterday,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.442
so this is like the best gift ever.

00:03:19.442 --> 00:03:20.616
(audience applauds)

00:03:20.616 --> 00:03:21.857
- Wow.

00:03:21.857 --> 00:03:22.690
- [Megan] Yeah.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:23.704
- That's God looking out.

00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:25.440
Alright, that's amazing.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.273
- [Megan] So...

00:03:26.273 --> 00:03:27.210
- [Kelly] Well, enjoy the holidays

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.410
and that thousand dollars at least.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.316
That'll be fun.

00:03:29.316 --> 00:03:30.149
- That will be fun.

00:03:30.149 --> 00:03:30.990
- Well, happy holidays to you

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.030
and thank you so much to
all our guests this hour.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:33.863
(audience applauds)

00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:35.002
Anna Kendrick, Jordan L. Jones,

00:03:35.002 --> 00:03:36.938
Duff Goldman, Sasha and Coco Jones.

00:03:36.938 --> 00:03:38.296
Y'all have a wonderful day.

00:03:38.296 --> 00:03:40.830
And if it's not, try and change it.

